+# Contract: `splitter` command-line interface
+
+**Feature**: `001-expense-splitter` | **Date**: 2026-11-03
+
+This is the **normative** interface — the only one users and calling scripts depend on. Changing
+anything below is a breaking change. Every item is traced to the requirement that fixes it.
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m splitter EXPENSES.csv --participants NAMES
+```
+
+Run from the repository root with `src` on the import path:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m splitter expenses.csv --participants "Alice,Bob"
+```
+
+| Element | Required | Contract |
+|---------|----------|----------|
+| `EXPENSES.csv` | yes | Exactly one positional argument: the path of the expenses file (FR-001) |
+| `--participants NAMES` | yes | Comma-separated participant names (FR-001) |
+| `prog` name in messages | — | `splitter` |
+
+More than one positional argument, a missing positional, a missing `--participants`, or any
+unrecognised option is a command-line error (exit 2, below). No other options exist; no
+configuration file or environment variable alters behaviour.
+
+## Input: expenses file
+
+| Property | Contract | Requirement |
+|----------|----------|-------------|
+| Encoding | UTF-8; a leading byte-order mark is ignored; undecodable bytes are an error | FR-002a |
+| Format | Comma-separated, standard double-quote quoting (so descriptions may contain commas) | FR-002 |
+| Header | First non-blank line must be exactly `payer,amount,description` — that order, lower case, no extra columns, no surrounding spaces in the field names | FR-002 |
+| Data rows | Each subsequent non-blank line is one expense with exactly three fields | FR-002, FR-010 |
+| Blank lines | Ignored anywhere in the file; a trailing newline is normal | Assumptions |
+| Amount grammar | Digits, optional single decimal point followed by one or two digits, optional leading `+`; surrounding whitespace ignored. Valid: `30`, `30.5`, `30.00`, `0`, `0.00`, `+30`. Invalid: `abc`, ``, `-5.00`, `1.005`, `$5`, `1,200.00`, `1e3`, `inf`, `nan`, `3 0.00` | FR-003, FR-004 |
+| Payer | Must equal one of the participants exactly after trimming, case-sensitively | FR-006 |
+| Description | Read for the field count, then ignored; never affects output | FR-018 |
+| File mutation | None. The file is opened read-only and is byte-identical after every run | FR-021, SC-008 |
+
+## Input: participant list
+
+| Rule | Contract | Requirement |
+|------|----------|-------------|
+| Splitting | Split the value on commas; trim surrounding whitespace from each element | FR-006 |
+| Non-empty | At least one name must result | FR-007 |
+| No empty element | `Alice,,Bob` and `Alice,Bob,` are errors, never silently skipped | FR-007 |
+| No duplicates | The same trimmed name twice is an error | FR-008 |
+| Case | Case-sensitive: `alice` and `Alice` are two people | FR-006 |
+| Ordering | Where order matters, ascending Unicode code-point order of the trimmed name; no locale collation, case-folding, or accent-folding; identical under every `LC_*` setting | FR-011a, SC-005 |
+
+## Output: standard output on success
+
+One line per payment, in the order the settlement algorithm generates them (FR-015):
+
+```text
+PAYER pays PAYEE AMOUNT
+```
+
+| Property | Contract | Requirement |
+|----------|----------|-------------|
+| Separator | Single spaces; the literal word `pays` | FR-016 |
+| Amount | Exactly two decimal places, no currency symbol, no thousands separator, no sign | FR-016 |
+| Minimum amount | Every printed amount is at least `0.01`; a `0.00` line never appears | FR-013 |
+| Line count | At most (number of participants − 1) | FR-013, SC-003 |
+| Conservation | The printed amounts sum to exactly the total imbalance | FR-014, SC-002 |
+| Already settled | Nothing at all is printed (no header, no "nothing to do" message) | FR-017 |
+| Determinism | Byte-identical across repeated runs and across locales | FR-015, SC-005 |
+| Line ending | `\n` after every line, including the last |  |
+
+Reference case (SC-001) — file `payer,amount,description` + `Alice,30.00,Hotel`, participants
+`Alice,Bob`:
+
+```text
+Bob pays Alice 15.00
+```
+
+## Output: standard error and exit status on failure
+
+On any failure: **exactly one** message on stderr, **nothing** on stdout, non-zero exit (FR-019,
+FR-020). Where an input holds several problems, only the first is reported and the tool stops there
+(FR-010a, SC-004).
+
+| Exit | Meaning | Requirement |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| 0 | Success, including the already-settled case | FR-017, FR-020 |
+| 1 | Input or validation failure (every row in the table below) | FR-019, FR-020 |
+| 2 | Malformed command line — missing path, missing `--participants`, unrecognised option, extra positional. `argparse` prints its usage line and the `splitter: error: …` message | FR-020 |
+
+### Message catalogue (exit 1)
+
+Every message is prefixed `splitter: error: ` on stderr, and names the problem plus — where the
+problem lies in the file — the line number and the offending value (SC-007). `{path}` is the path as
+the user typed it; `{line}` is the 1-based physical line number.
+
+| Condition | Message | Requirement |
+|-----------|---------|-------------|
+| Empty participant list | `--participants requires at least one participant name` | FR-007 |
+| Empty element in list | `--participants contains an empty participant name` | FR-007 |
+| Duplicate participant | `--participants contains duplicate participant name '{name}'` | FR-008 |
+| File missing or unreadable | `cannot read expenses file '{path}': {reason}` | FR-009 |
+| Not valid UTF-8 | `cannot decode expenses file '{path}' as UTF-8` | FR-002a |
+| No header (file empty or all blank) | `{path}: missing header row; expected 'payer,amount,description'` | FR-002, FR-010 |
+| Wrong header | `{path}:{line}: header must be exactly 'payer,amount,description'; found '{found}'` | FR-002, FR-010 |
+| Wrong field count | `{path}:{line}: expected 3 fields, found {count}` | FR-010 |
+| Unknown payer | `{path}:{line}: unknown payer '{payer}'; not in the participant list` | FR-006 |
+| Invalid amount | `{path}:{line}: invalid amount '{value}'; expected a non-negative number with at most two decimal places` | FR-003, FR-004 |
+
+`{found}` renders the header row's fields re-joined with commas, so the user sees what their file
+actually says. For a multi-line quoted record, `{line}` is the record's last physical line.
+
+### Order of checks
+
+Fail-fast, stopping at the first problem (FR-010a):
+
+1. Command line shape (`argparse`) → exit 2
+2. Participant list: empty → empty element → duplicate
+3. Opening and decoding the file
+4. Header
+5. Data rows by increasing line number; within one row: field count → payer → amount
+
+So a file with a bad amount on line 3 and an unknown payer on line 5 reports only the line 3 amount;
+a bad header hides every row problem; and a duplicate participant is reported without the file being
+opened at all.
+
+## Guarantees
+
+| Guarantee | Requirement |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| No third-party import at runtime | Constitution I |
+| No file created, modified, or deleted; no network access | FR-021, SC-008 |
+| Results on stdout, diagnostics on stderr, never interleaved | Constitution Interfaces |
+| 1,000 rows × 50 participants completes in under two seconds | SC-006 |
+| Identical input always yields identical output and exit status | FR-015, SC-005 |
